is  seeking treatment from a therapist  played by Naomi Watts a woman with her  own set of issues as Alison gets deeper  into her treatment gene struggles to  stay within the typical boundaries that  exist between a counselor and her  patient Boyton talked to Entertainment  Weekly about the experience of making  the show saying she was drawn to the  dark project because the writing allows  viewers to see quote the truest dirtiest  sides of people  speaking of dark projects director Polly  Steel's letmego was crowdfunded and  based on the autobiographical book of  the same name by Helga Schneider about  learning that her estranged mother had  been a guard at a Nazi concentration  camp the film tells the story from the  perspective of Helga who at age 60  receives a letter detailing her aging  mother's whereabouts along with her  daughter Beth and granddaughter Emily  played by Boynton Helga travels to  Vienna to see her mother one last time  where she finds the matriarch  remorseless about her role in the  Holocaust Catcher in the Rye author JD  Salinger was a notorious recluse until  his death in 2010 and refused to allow a  film adaptation of his novel to be made  saying it was quote unactive or director  Danny strong attempted the next best  thing with rebel and the RAI which  chronicles the life of Salinger as he  wrote the landmark novel Nicholas how to  plays a young Salinger who along the way  meets Clare Douglas played by Boynton in  real life Douglass was the inspiration  for Franny glass the character featured  in Salinger's Franny and Zooey poorer  films were a hallmark of Lucy Boynton's  early career don't knock twice like  letmego is a story about mothers and  daughters except with way more ghosts  Boynton plays Chloe a teenager who  unwittingly awakens a witch living in an  abandoned house in an effort to escape  the evil Chloe flees to the country to  stay with her estranged mother Jess Jess  is a successful artist who lives with  her lawyer husband and now wants to  reconnect with her daughter after  previously losing her to foster care  because of a substance abuse problem but  the witch problem they're all facing now  may prove worse I am the pretty thing  that lives in the house was the second  collaboration between Boynton and  director Osgood Oz Perkins the son of  psycho star Anthony Perkins much like  his father's most famous flick the movie  centers on a dwelling where creepy  things happen in this case it's the 200  year old New England home of iris Blum a  popular author of horror novels things  get weird when Miss Blum's new nurse  Lily realizes that the old woman is  talking to someone named Polly who  doesn't appear to be there or is she  point in place Polly the main character  of the lady in the wall one of Blum's  novels from decades ago but it's  possible that Polly is more than just a  fictional character  and flashbacks Polly is seen as a young  woman condemned to a terrible fate Singh  Street was Boynton's first lead acting  role having been previously relegated to  supporting characters the musical story  about a teenager in Dublin trying to  start a band in order to impress a girl  was popular at Sundance when it  premiered in 2016 and was nominated for  Golden Globe for Best Picture Musical or  Comedy never do anything by half  Boynton plays Rufina an aspiring model  being wooed by fourteen-year-old Conor  Cosmo la loire for Boyton the film was a  new experience it was one of the few  times in her young career that she was  one of the oldest actors on set in 2015  Boynton teamed up with director oz  Perkins for the first time in the black  coats daughter a film that was  originally called February when it made  its premiere at the Toronto Film  Festival after being held in release  date limbo for more than a year the  movie hit streaming services with a new  title in the movie Cats  played by Keanu Shipka and Rose played  by Boynton are stuck at a Catholic girls  boarding school when a mysterious young  woman arrives before too long captain  Rose are left to battle and unforeseen  evil copperhead is a period drama that  was only boynton second film credits in  the movie  Boynton plays ester Hagedorn daughter of  a hardline upstate New York abolitionist  during the Civil War  ester falls in love with Jeff beech the  son of a pacifist the vast political  difference between the lovers fathers  threatens to derail their relationship  the movie was based on the book the  Copperhead by Harold Frederick which  examined the differing political  attitudes that existed on the homefront  during America's Civil War Boynton made  her big screen debut in miss Potter at  the age of eleven she was cast as a  young Beatrix Potter the famed author  who created the Tale of Peter Rabbit and  a number of other classic children's  books with charming animal characters it  didn't take long for young Lucy to be  bitten by the acting bug  she told WWD that on her first day on  the set of miss Potter she decided that  nothing else quote could make her as  happy or feel as fulfilled as acting  does so they say check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite actors  are coming soon so  scribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  you
 

